KG42.register("edges-3b9b0b262ae0f28f4ef41312",{"id":"S-08125d031225f6a2","source":"COMP-5e870d267afec9a0","type":"links","target":"COMP-ab3d11c48c98c7be","evidence_class":"S","scientific_acceptance":false,"relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"paper_ids":["02-dlmp","08-real_time_prices"],"assertions":[{"id":"02-dlmp::v141-c-R006::E::v141-c-R006-E001","paper":"02-dlmp","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","rule_ref":"02-dlmp::v141-c-R006","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R006-E001","source":"clearing.social_welfare","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E01","v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g01-E14"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R006-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-5e870d267afec9a0","target":"COMP-ab3d11c48c98c7be","source_occurrence_id":"02-dlmp::v141-c-R006::V::clearing.social_welfare","target_occurrence_id":"02-dlmp::v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","source_unit_id":"02-dlmp::v141-a-M01::clearing.social_welfare","target_unit_id":"02-dlmp::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"DLMP price decomposition under the RBTS simplification. | Distribution-network DLMP calculation in the proposed DSO procedure. | Next-day DLMP formation in the local DSO market.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E01","v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E37"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"21d338de580bf679be896d668f0b9d6a3cbcc16f103fa6f2bf6ce749ddfe552e","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"Economic objective and its applicability in this mechanism: DSO network-constrained welfare dispatch with elastic demand and price-taking EV aggregators; posted next-day DLMPs coordinate conditional decentralized response.","target_definition":"DSO welfare optimization forms next-day locational prices. Under the stated RBTS generation-PTDF and interior conventional-demand assumptions, DLMP equals the reference LMP plus locational congestion markup; retain the conditions and unclosed KKT gaps.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Constrained social-welfare optimization of the electric distribution system determines the next-day DLMPs. Scope: Next-day DLMP formation in the local DSO market. Condition: EV aggregators are modeled as price takers and demand price elasticity is included.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.social_welfare","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E01","v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g01-E14"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E01","location":{"location_id":"src-16569f9a14-p01-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":1,"printed_page":"203","section":"Abstract","anchor_text":"Abstract This paper presents an integrated distribution lo cational marginal pricing (DLMP) method d","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"In the proposed approach, the distribution system operator (DSO) determines distribution locational marginal prices (DLMPs) by solving the social welfare optimization of the electric distribution system which considers EV aggregators as price takers in the local DSO market and demand price elasticity."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E08","location":{"location_id":"src-16569f9a14-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":2,"printed_page":"204","section":"II. Determination of DLMPs Using Integrated Optimization","anchor_text":"and PowerWorld [19]. ere The DCOPF was adopted in the derivation of DLMPs as a to practical approach","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"The DCOPF was adopted in the derivation of DLMPs as a practical approach to address the computational complexity resulting from the large number of nodes within the electric distribution network. In the proposed DLMP algorithm, the DSO determines the DLMPs for the next day by solving a constrained social welfare maximization problem."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E14","location":{"location_id":"src-16569f9a14-p03-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":"205","section":"II. Determination of DLMPs Using Integrated Optimization","anchor_text":"( ) beneﬁt of the EV demand is not included in the objective func- tion since that component is cons","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"The objective function consists of two components, social value of meeting the conventional demand, given by the area under the demand functions, and the cost of satisfying both the EV demand and the conventional demand, as shown in (1). The benefit of the EV demand is not included in the objective function since that component is constant, as long as the EV demand is met within the day, and is not affected by the charging schedule. Instead, a constraint requiring that the EV demand be met by the schedule is included. To be more specific, the object function in (1) can be further decomposed into three terms as shown by"}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"DLMP price decomposition under the RBTS simplification. | Distribution-network DLMP calculation in the proposed DSO procedure. | Next-day DLMP formation in the local DSO market.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E01","v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E37"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R006-E001","source":"clearing.social_welfare","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E01","v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g01-E14"]},"paper_scope_note":"Distinguish centralized DLMP construction by the DSO from decentralized response implementing the configuration; achieving optimality must retain price acceptance and the condition that the demand non-negativity constraint is non-binding, and the result cannot be used to prove algorithmic component dependencies in reverse."}},{"id":"08-real_time_prices::v141-c-R004::E::v141-c-R004-E002","paper":"08-real_time_prices","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","rule_ref":"08-real_time_prices::v141-c-R004","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E002","source":"clearing.social_welfare","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev-17","v141-b-g02-ev-22"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004-C003"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-5e870d267afec9a0","target":"COMP-ab3d11c48c98c7be","source_occurrence_id":"08-real_time_prices::v141-c-R004::V::clearing.social_welfare","target_occurrence_id":"08-real_time_prices::v141-c-R004::V::coordination.price_signal","source_unit_id":"08-real_time_prices::v141-a-M01::clearing.social_welfare","target_unit_id":"08-real_time_prices::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Alignment of price signals with measurement and settlement intervals. | Current RP bid-submission deadlines and EcoGrid real-time price announcements for the same operational hour. | Day-ahead spot-price signals published in the real-time marketplace for the following day. | Delivery of EcoGrid real-time coordination prices. | EcoGrid EU's specified five-minute market design. | EcoGrid real-time coordination price for an operational hour. | EcoGrid real-time price-setting design. | Price-responsive behavior represented in the proposed model's supply-demand balance constraint (2). | Proposed anti-arbitrage rules separating RP and real-time market participation. | Proposed multi-period stochastic optimization over the study horizon. | Publication of real-time signals during operation of the five-minute market. | Short-term production and consumption planning by market participants. | Single-period TSO optimization for balancing at the next time step. | Stated infrastructure prerequisites for implementing the proposed price-responsive market. | Timing of decentralized actions responding to EcoGrid real-time prices.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev11","v141-b-g01-ev12","v141-b-g01-ev15","v141-b-g01-ev22","v141-b-g01-ev23","v141-b-g01-ev24","v141-b-g01-ev30","v141-b-g02-ev-16","v141-b-g02-ev-17","v141-b-g02-ev-22","v141-b-g03-e10"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"61e2e929dc4209e3acdec0aed40605711251614757ee205a423b703942430c9e","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"Economic objective and its applicability in this mechanism: TSO stochastic balancing optimization posts five-minute prices; small consumers/DERs respond without bids or schedules and without obligations to deliver assumed response.","target_definition":"TSO sets and publishes the next five-minute response price using operating status and single-period or scenario-based welfare optimization; absence of imbalance/congestion gives the day-ahead price. Keep planning-only next-day signals, forecasts and metering alignment as distinct contextual branches.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The social-welfare optimization determines the real-time price used for price-signal coordination at the next time step. Scope: Single-period TSO optimization for balancing at the next time step. Condition: When the proposed single-period optimization model is used.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.social_welfare","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["lambda_R"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev-17"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The optimization maximizing expected social welfare determines the real-time price and price forecasts for price-signal coordination. Scope: Proposed multi-period stochastic optimization over the study horizon. Condition: When the proposed multi-period stochastic optimization model is used.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.social_welfare","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["lambda_R"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev-22"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-ev-17","location":{"location_id":"src-da8e4e26d6-p06-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-A. Real-Time Price Settlement Model","anchor_text":"The objective function (3), shown at the bottom of the page, aims to minimize the regulating power c","equation_id":"Eq. (4)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The TSO will use the following single-period optimization model for the deployment of up and down regulating power and determination of real-time price for maintaining the system balance for the next time step $(t = 1)$. The objective function (3), shown at the bottom of the page, aims to minimize the regulating power cost taking into account the prosumer' response (demand and DERs) to real-time price signals, which aims to minimize the total social cost (equivalent to maximization of social welfare). Note that the costs of load shedding and wind spillage are also considered. In the prosumer' response model, a linear correlation between the electricity consumption or generation of an aggregation of prosumers (consumers or DERs) and the real-time electricity price is considered, which have been used in most technical literature [10]–[12]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-ev-22","location":{"location_id":"src-da8e4e26d6-p07-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Real-Time Price Settlement and Forecast Model","anchor_text":"time step and price forecasts at time step is for different possible scenarios. The TSO also de- lus","equation_id":"Eq. (14)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In real life, only a real-time price signal for the next ﬁve minute may not be sufﬁcient for market players for scheduling their production or consumption in an optimal way. Short-term and accurate real-time price forecast (e.g., price forecast for the operational hour) based on the predicted requirements of balancing power can be delivered to market players for optimally adjusting their production or consumption planning. Inspired by that, a multi-period optimization model for determining real-time price and price forecast should also be developed. Uncertain parameters such as wind production and aggregated response of consumers and DERs to real-time electricity prices are approximated by a set of scenarios with their corresponding probabilities of occurrence. The TSO will use the following multi-period stochastic optimization model for determining the real-time price at the next time step $(t = 1)$ and price forecasts at time step $t(\\forall t = 2, \\ldots, N_t)$ for different possible scenarios. The TSO also determines the deployment of up and down regulating power at the next time step $(t = 1)$ and time step $t(\\forall t = 2, \\ldots, N_t)$ for all possible scenarios respectively. The objective function of the proposed model will then be the maximization of the expected social welfare throughout the study horizon, i.e., the minimization of the reserve deployment cost by the generators and DERs for providing balancing power plus wind spillage cost minus the utility losses of the consumers. As shown in (14) at the bottom of the page, the objective function includes two items. The ﬁrst item represents the corresponding cost at next time step $(t = 1)$, which is the same as (4). The second item represents the expected cost incurred from time step $t = 2$ to time step $t = N_t$. The objective function (14) is subject to constraints (2), (4)–(13) and following constraints:"}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Alignment of price signals with measurement and settlement intervals. | Current RP bid-submission deadlines and EcoGrid real-time price announcements for the same operational hour. | Day-ahead spot-price signals published in the real-time marketplace for the following day. | Delivery of EcoGrid real-time coordination prices. | EcoGrid EU's specified five-minute market design. | EcoGrid real-time coordination price for an operational hour. | EcoGrid real-time price-setting design. | Price-responsive behavior represented in the proposed model's supply-demand balance constraint (2). | Proposed anti-arbitrage rules separating RP and real-time market participation. | Proposed multi-period stochastic optimization over the study horizon. | Publication of real-time signals during operation of the five-minute market. | Short-term production and consumption planning by market participants. | Single-period TSO optimization for balancing at the next time step. | Stated infrastructure prerequisites for implementing the proposed price-responsive market. | Timing of decentralized actions responding to EcoGrid real-time prices.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev11","v141-b-g01-ev12","v141-b-g01-ev15","v141-b-g01-ev22","v141-b-g01-ev23","v141-b-g01-ev24","v141-b-g01-ev30","v141-b-g02-ev-16","v141-b-g02-ev-17","v141-b-g02-ev-22","v141-b-g03-e10"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E002","source":"clearing.social_welfare","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev-17","v141-b-g02-ev-22"]},"paper_scope_note":"Single-period and multi-period optimization are kept separate; RP bidders and quote-free responders are kept separate; temporal precedence is not treated as mechanism necessity."}}],"assertion_ids":["02-dlmp::v141-c-R006::E::v141-c-R006-E001","08-real_time_prices::v141-c-R004::E::v141-c-R004-E002"]});
